From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 03:33:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(backend): implement document (PDF) forensics module

Replace the Phase 1 document stub with rule-based PDF forensics that
returns the shared ModuleResult schema:

- Metadata: creator/producer/author/title, Info vs XMP mismatch
- Timeline: modified-after-created, modified-before-created, future dates
- Editor software trail in Producer/Creator
- Raw bytes: %%EOF / startxref / /Prev counts -> incremental updates;
  digital signatures lower the severity (signing adds a revision)
- Overlays: white-filled rectangles + mixed font families, extra
  content streams, annotations, form fields
- Optional PyMuPDF text-span check for font changes inside one line

Findings are only created for medium/high indicators and each links
to its Evidence. model_confidence stays None (no neural detector).

Also: mark document_forensics as completed in /api/v1/modules and
/health, add pypdf + pymupdf to requirements, and add 5 tests that
build tiny fictional PDFs in memory (no binaries committed).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
